<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE module PUBLIC
          "-//Checkstyle//DTD Checkstyle Configuration 1.3//EN"
          "https://checkstyle.org/dtds/configuration_1_3.dtd">

<!--
    Checkstyle configuration for the `best-practice-java` skill.

    Derived from the Checkstyle project's `google_checks.xml`
    (https://github.com/checkstyle/checkstyle/blob/master/src/main/resources/google_checks.xml),
    which encodes the Google Java Style Guide
    (https://google.github.io/styleguide/javaguide.html).

    ===========================================================================
    WHAT THIS CONFIG DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CHECK
    ===========================================================================
    Every formatting concern is owned by google-java-format (run via Spotless).
    Running the same rule in two tools produces duplicate findings, and worse,
    findings a developer cannot fix without fighting the formatter. So all of
    the following modules present in upstream google_checks.xml are removed
    here on purpose:

      Indentation, LineLength, FileTabCharacter, RegexpSingleline (trailing
      whitespace), WhitespaceAfter, WhitespaceAround, WhitespaceBeforeEmptyBody,
      NoWhitespaceBefore, NoWhitespaceBeforeCaseDefaultColon,
      SingleSpaceSeparator, GenericWhitespace, MethodParamPad, ParenPad,
      OperatorWrap, SeparatorWrap, LeftCurly, RightCurly, EmptyLineSeparator,
      NoLineWrap, CommentsIndentation, AnnotationLocation,
      JavadocContentLocation, JavadocLeadingAsteriskAlign,
      JavadocMissingLeadingAsterisk, JavadocTagContinuationIndentation,
      JavadocParagraph, RequireEmptyLineBeforeBlockTagGroup,
      TextBlockGoogleStyleFormatting.

    See chapter 1 (Formatting & Tooling) and chapter 38 (Static Analysis
    Configuration) of the best-practice-java skill for the full rationale.

    ===========================================================================
    A NOTE ON MissingSwitchDefault AND EXHAUSTIVENESS
    ===========================================================================
    `MissingSwitchDefault` IS enabled, but its scope is narrower than its name
    suggests, and the difference matters for Java 21 code.

    Google Java Style section 4.8.4.3 requires every switch to be *exhaustive*.
    It states that a switch is exhaustive "if it has a `default` label, but also
    for example if the value being switched on is an enum and every value of the
    enum is matched by a switch label." A `default` label is therefore one route
    to exhaustiveness, not the only one.

    Per the check's own documentation, `MissingSwitchDefault`:
      - does NOT validate switch *expressions* (javac already proves those
        exhaustive), and
      - does NOT validate switch statements using pattern or null labels
        (javac proves those exhaustive too).

    So it does not fight pattern switches over `sealed` hierarchies, which is
    the idiom chapters 13, 14, and 23 teach. What it does still flag is an
    old-style colon-form statement switch over an enum that already matches
    every constant. That is the one place the check and this skill disagree:
    adding a `default` there converts what should become a compile error when a
    new enum constant is introduced into a silent runtime fallthrough.

    The resolution is to write that switch as a switch *expression* with arrow
    labels, which chapter 23 requires anyway and which the check exempts. Where
    an old-style exhaustive enum switch genuinely must stay, suppress it at the
    declaration with a reason:

        @SuppressWarnings("checkstyle:MissingSwitchDefault") // exhaustive; a
        // new constant must break the build here rather than fall through

    `FallThrough` below still catches the classic old-style switch bug.

    ===========================================================================
    SUPPRESSION POLICY
    ===========================================================================
    Suppress with a narrowly scoped annotation and a comment explaining why:

        @SuppressWarnings("checkstyle:AbbreviationAsWordInName") // JNI naming
        native int readFD(int fd);

    File-level suppressions go in `checkstyle-suppressions.xml` next to this
    file. Never suppress at the Checker level. Never suppress without a reason.
-->

<module name="Checker">

  <property name="charset" value="UTF-8"/>

  <!-- Fail the build by default. Override with -Dcheckstyle.severity=warning
       during an incremental migration of an existing codebase. -->
  <property name="severity" value="${checkstyle.severity}" default="error"/>

  <property name="fileExtensions" value="java, properties, xml"/>

  <!-- module-info.java has its own grammar and its own conventions. -->
  <module name="BeforeExecutionExclusionFileFilter">
    <property name="fileNamePattern" value="module\-info\.java$"/>
  </module>

  <!-- Honours @SuppressWarnings("checkstyle:CheckName") on declarations. -->
  <module name="SuppressWarningsFilter"/>

  <!-- Optional file-based suppressions; absent file is not an error. -->
  <module name="SuppressionFilter">
    <property name="file" value="${checkstyle.suppressions.file}"
              default="config/checkstyle/checkstyle-suppressions.xml"/>
    <property name="optional" value="true"/>
  </module>

  <module name="NewlineAtEndOfFile"/>

  <module name="TreeWalker">

    <!-- Required for SuppressWarningsFilter above to see the annotations. -->
    <module name="SuppressWarningsHolder"/>

    <!-- =================================================================
         Source file structure  (Google Java Style sections 2 and 3)
         Skill chapter 2.
         ================================================================= -->

    <!-- section 2.1: file name matches the top-level class name -->
    <module name="OuterTypeFilename"/>

    <!-- section 3.4.1: exactly one top-level class per file -->
    <module name="OneTopLevelClass"/>

    <!-- section 3.3.1: no wildcard imports -->
    <module name="AvoidStarImport"/>

    <!-- section 3.3.3: static group first, then non-static, each ASCII-sorted -->
    <module name="CustomImportOrder">
      <property name="sortImportsInGroupAlphabetically" value="true"/>
      <property name="separateLineBetweenGroups" value="true"/>
      <property name="customImportOrderRules" value="STATIC###THIRD_PARTY_PACKAGE"/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 2.3.2: prefer special escape sequences to octal/Unicode escapes -->
    <module name="IllegalTokenText">
      <property name="tokens" value="STRING_LITERAL, CHAR_LITERAL, TEXT_BLOCK_CONTENT"/>
      <property name="format"
                value="\\u00(08|09|0(a|A)|0(c|C)|0(d|D)|20|22|27|5(C|c))|\\(0(10|11|12|14|15|40|42|47)|134)"/>
      <property name="message"
                value="Consider using special escape sequence instead of octal value or Unicode escaped value."/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 2.3.3: non-ASCII characters -->
    <module name="AvoidEscapedUnicodeCharacters">
      <property name="allowEscapesForControlCharacters" value="true"/>
      <property name="allowByTailComment" value="true"/>
      <property name="allowNonPrintableEscapes" value="true"/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 3.4.2.1: overloads are never split by another member -->
    <module name="OverloadMethodsDeclarationOrder"/>

    <!-- constructors are declared as a contiguous group -->
    <module name="ConstructorsDeclarationGrouping"/>

    <!-- =================================================================
         Naming  (Google Java Style section 5)
         Skill chapter 3.
         ================================================================= -->

    <module name="PackageName">
      <property name="format" value="^[a-z]+(\.[a-z][a-z0-9]*)*$"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Package name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <module name="TypeName">
      <property name="format" value="^[A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9]*(?:[0-9](?:_[0-9]+)*)?$"/>
      <property name="tokens" value="CLASS_DEF"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Type name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <!-- Underscores are permitted in JUnit test method names (section 5.2.3). -->
    <module name="MethodName">
      <property name="format"
                value="^(?![a-z]$)(?![a-z][A-Z])[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[A-Z][a-z0-9]*)*(?:_[0-9]+)*$"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Method name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 5.2.5: non-constant fields are lowerCamelCase, no m/s/k prefixes -->
    <module name="GoogleNonConstantFieldName"/>

    <module name="ParameterName">
      <property name="format" value="^[a-z]([a-z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9]*)?$"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Parameter name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 5.2.9: `_` is permitted for unnamed variables and parameters -->
    <module name="LambdaParameterName">
      <property name="format" value="^(_|[a-z]([a-z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9]*)?)$"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Lambda parameter name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <module name="CatchParameterName">
      <property name="format" value="^(_|[a-z]([a-z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9]*)?)$"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Catch parameter name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <module name="LocalVariableName">
      <property name="format" value="^(_|[a-z]([a-z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9]*)?)$"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Local variable name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <module name="LocalFinalVariableName">
      <property name="format" value="^(_|[a-z]([a-z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9]*)?)$"/>
      <property name="tokens" value="VARIABLE_DEF, PARAMETER_DEF, RESOURCE"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Local final variable name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <module name="PatternVariableName">
      <property name="format" value="^(_|[a-z]([a-z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9]*)?)$"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Pattern variable name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <module name="RecordComponentName">
      <property name="format" value="^[a-z]([a-z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9]*)?$"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Record component name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 5.2.8: a single capital letter optionally followed by a
         numeral, or a class-style name followed by a capital T -->
    <module name="ClassTypeParameterName">
      <property name="format" value="(^[A-Z][0-9]?$)|(^[A-Z]T$)|(^([A-Z][a-z0-9]+)+T$)"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Class type name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <module name="RecordTypeParameterName">
      <property name="format" value="(^[A-Z][0-9]?$)|(^[A-Z]T$)|(^([A-Z][a-z0-9]+)+T$)"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Record type name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <module name="MethodTypeParameterName">
      <property name="format" value="(^[A-Z][0-9]?$)|(^[A-Z]T$)|(^([A-Z][a-z0-9]+)+T$)"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Method type name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <module name="InterfaceTypeParameterName">
      <property name="format" value="(^[A-Z][0-9]?$)|(^[A-Z]T$)|(^([A-Z][a-z0-9]+)+T$)"/>
      <message key="name.invalidPattern"
               value="Interface type name ''{0}'' must match pattern ''{1}''."/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 5.3: camel case algorithm — XmlHttpRequest, not XMLHTTPRequest -->
    <module name="AbbreviationAsWordInName">
      <property name="ignoreFinal" value="false"/>
      <property name="allowedAbbreviationLength" value="0"/>
      <property name="tokens"
                value="CLASS_DEF, INTERFACE_DEF, ENUM_DEF, ANNOTATION_DEF, ANNOTATION_FIELD_DEF,
                       PARAMETER_DEF, VARIABLE_DEF, METHOD_DEF, PATTERN_VARIABLE_DEF, RECORD_DEF,
                       RECORD_COMPONENT_DEF"/>
    </module>

    <!-- =================================================================
         Programming practices  (Google Java Style section 6)
         Skill chapters 6, 7, 23.
         ================================================================= -->

    <!-- section 4.8.7: canonical modifier order -->
    <module name="ModifierOrder"/>

    <!-- section 6.4: do not override Object.finalize -->
    <module name="NoFinalizer"/>

    <!-- section 4.1.1: braces are used even where optional -->
    <module name="NeedBraces">
      <property name="tokens"
                value="LITERAL_DO, LITERAL_ELSE, LITERAL_FOR, LITERAL_IF, LITERAL_WHILE"/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 6.2: a caught exception is never silently ignored; an empty
         catch block must carry a comment explaining why that is correct -->
    <module name="EmptyCatchBlock">
      <property name="commentFormat" value="\w+"/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 4.3 -->
    <module name="OneStatementPerLine"/>

    <!-- section 4.8.2.1 -->
    <module name="MultipleVariableDeclarations"/>

    <!-- section 4.8.3.2: no C-style `String args[]` declarations -->
    <module name="ArrayTypeStyle"/>

    <!-- section 4.8.4.2: old-style switch fall-through must be commented -->
    <module name="FallThrough"/>

    <!-- section 4.8.4.3: exhaustiveness. Exempts switch expressions and
         pattern/null-label switches, which javac already proves exhaustive.
         See the header note for the one enum case where it disagrees with
         chapter 23. -->
    <module name="MissingSwitchDefault"/>

    <!-- section 4.8.8: long literals use uppercase L -->
    <module name="UpperEll"/>

    <!-- section 4.8.2.2: declare locals close to first use -->
    <module name="VariableDeclarationUsageDistance"/>

    <!-- Java 21: a record accessor that is explicitly declared is an override -->
    <module name="MissingOverrideOnRecordAccessor"/>

    <!-- section 4.8.6.2: TODO comments are all-caps and followed by a colon -->
    <module name="TodoComment">
      <property name="id" value="TodoFormat"/>
      <property name="format" value="^[ \t]*(?!TODO:)(?i:TODO)\b:?"/>
      <message key="todo.match"
               value="''TODO:'' must be written in all caps and followed by a colon."/>
    </module>

    <!-- =================================================================
         Javadoc  (Google Java Style section 7)
         Skill chapter 4. Formatting-only Javadoc checks are omitted; these
         are the ones google-java-format cannot decide for you.
         ================================================================= -->

    <module name="InvalidJavadocPosition"/>

    <module name="JavadocMethod">
      <property name="accessModifiers" value="public"/>
      <property name="allowMissingParamTags" value="true"/>
      <property name="allowMissingReturnTag" value="true"/>
      <property name="allowedAnnotations" value="Override, Test"/>
      <property name="tokens" value="METHOD_DEF, CTOR_DEF, ANNOTATION_FIELD_DEF, COMPACT_CTOR_DEF"/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 7.3: Javadoc present for every visible member, with the
         self-explanatory and override exceptions of 7.3.1 and 7.3.2 -->
    <module name="MissingJavadocMethod">
      <property name="scope" value="protected"/>
      <property name="allowMissingPropertyJavadoc" value="true"/>
      <property name="allowedAnnotations" value="Override, Test"/>
      <property name="tokens" value="METHOD_DEF, CTOR_DEF, ANNOTATION_FIELD_DEF, COMPACT_CTOR_DEF"/>
    </module>

    <module name="MissingJavadocType">
      <property name="scope" value="protected"/>
      <property name="tokens"
                value="CLASS_DEF, INTERFACE_DEF, ENUM_DEF, RECORD_DEF, ANNOTATION_DEF"/>
      <property name="excludeScope" value="nothing"/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 7.1.3: @param, @return, @throws, @deprecated, in that order,
         and never with an empty description -->
    <module name="AtclauseOrder">
      <property name="tagOrder" value="@param, @return, @throws, @deprecated"/>
      <property name="target"
                value="CLASS_DEF, INTERFACE_DEF, ENUM_DEF, METHOD_DEF, CTOR_DEF,
                       VARIABLE_DEF, RECORD_DEF, COMPACT_CTOR_DEF"/>
    </module>

    <module name="NonEmptyAtclauseDescription"/>

    <!-- section 7.2: the summary is a fragment, not a sentence. Rejects
         "This method returns ...", "A {@code Foo} is a ...", and a
         lowercase opening. -->
    <module name="SummaryJavadoc">
      <property name="forbiddenSummaryFragments"
                value="^@return the *|^This method returns |^A [{]@code [a-zA-Z0-9]+[}]( is a )|^[a-z]"/>
    </module>

    <!-- section 7.1.1: the single-line form is only valid without block tags -->
    <module name="SingleLineJavadoc"/>

    <!-- =================================================================
         BEYOND GOOGLE'S OWN RULESET

         Google's guide is deliberately silent on most design questions, so
         upstream google_checks.xml is silent too. The checks below are NOT in
         google_checks.xml. Each one mechanically enforces a rule the skill
         states from Effective Java or the JLS, so that those chapters can
         carry an honest `> Enforced by:` callout instead of a bare opinion.
         The chapter each check backs is named alongside it.
         ================================================================= -->

    <!-- Naming: google_checks covers non-constant fields via
         GoogleNonConstantFieldName but has no constant rule. Chapter 3. -->
    <module name="ConstantName"/>

    <!-- Equality contracts. Chapter 10. -->
    <module name="EqualsHashCode"/>
    <module name="CovariantEquals"/>
    <module name="EqualsAvoidNull"/>
    <module name="StringLiteralEquality"/>

    <!-- Object creation and class design. Chapters 8 and 11. -->
    <module name="FinalClass"/>
    <module name="HideUtilityClassConstructor"/>
    <module name="IllegalInstantiation"/>
    <module name="InterfaceIsType"/>
    <module name="VisibilityModifier"/>

    <!-- Resource and finalizer discipline. Chapters 7 and 9. -->
    <module name="SuperFinalize"/>
    <module name="UnnecessarySemicolonInTryWithResources"/>

    <!-- Exception discipline: never catch or declare Throwable, Error, or
         bare RuntimeException across an API boundary. Chapter 24. -->
    <module name="IllegalCatch"/>
    <module name="IllegalThrows"/>

    <!-- Program to the interface, not the implementation. Chapter 20. -->
    <module name="IllegalType"/>

    <!-- Imports. Chapter 2. -->
    <module name="PackageDeclaration"/>
    <module name="UnusedImports"/>
    <module name="IllegalImport"/>

    <!-- Declaration hygiene. Chapters 6 and 22. -->
    <module name="ExplicitInitialization"/>
    <module name="RedundantModifier"/>
    <module name="ParameterAssignment"/>
    <module name="UnusedLocalVariable"/>
    <module name="ModifiedControlVariable"/>

    <!-- Long parameter lists are a design smell; chapter 22 gives the three
         fixes (split the method, parameter object, builder). Overrides are
         exempt because the signature is not the author's to change. -->
    <module name="ParameterNumber">
      <property name="max" value="7"/>
      <property name="ignoreOverriddenMethods" value="true"/>
    </module>

    <!-- Shadowing a field with a parameter or local. Constructor parameters
         and setter parameters are the idiomatic exception. Chapter 6. -->
    <module name="HiddenField">
      <property name="ignoreConstructorParameter" value="true"/>
      <property name="ignoreSetter" value="true"/>
      <property name="ignoreAbstractMethods" value="true"/>
    </module>

    <!-- Control flow and modern switch. Chapter 23.
         MissingSwitchDefault stays absent for the reason given in the header;
         these are the checks that push toward exhaustive pattern switches
         rather than away from them. -->
    <module name="InnerAssignment"/>
    <module name="SimplifyBooleanExpression"/>
    <module name="SimplifyBooleanReturn"/>
    <module name="UseEnhancedSwitch"/>
    <module name="MissingNullCaseInSwitch"/>
    <module name="WhenShouldBeUsed"/>

    <!-- Redundant null check before instanceof; pattern matching makes this
         even more common. Chapter 25. -->
    <module name="UnnecessaryNullCheckWithInstanceOf"/>

  </module>
</module>
